A||||21||Oreif||Side Scoops Installed! See Pics!!||||6||
Z||000000||Oreif||09-28-2001||11:43 AM||||I just finished installing the side scoops that Sage made. (Bought them thru 007DOUG)<BR>These look and install great!!!! Here is a very helpful hint. To install them like the factory, you need the plastic rivets. I bought a "Marson" Rivet Kit. (cost is $44.95 and kit # is 480001) It comes with the tool and 100 rivets in 5 different sizes. (You need 2 different sizes to install panels)<BR>It took about 2 hours to install them. <BR>They fit great and everything lined up with no problem. (see pics)<P>I'll take better pics if it gets sunny out this weekend. Black cars seem to photograph better in the sun than in a garage.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>If you want side scoops and want excellent quality of the product these are the best. <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sidescoops1.jpg">   <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">      <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B><P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-28-2001||12:05 PM||||Oreif,<P>The scoops look great. Where did you get the Marson kit? How does the airbox attach to the inside of the side scoop? What parts do you have to remove to install them? <P>TIA<BR>Rick 88||||reg||5
Z||000002||gargoyle||09-28-2001||12:08 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> Very Nice! I like how they blend in with the side of the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||webbee||09-28-2001||12:17 PM||||Wow those really are great looking! Is this a performance mod or for looks. Did you do both sides?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||09-28-2001||12:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rick 88:<BR><B>Oreif,<P>The scoops look great. Where did you get the Marson kit? How does the airbox attach to the inside of the side scoop? What parts do you have to remove to install them? <P>TIA<BR>Rick 88</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I bought the Marson kit at a body shop supply store. The air box is just open it doesn't attach to the scoop. I also removed the air obstruction panel inside the air box. The only parts you need to remove are the lower aero skirt (if equipped), the aero skirt upper piece on the panel (and attach it to the new panel) and the trim molding. The top edge of the panel slides under the sail panel and tucks under the top panel. You need to drill out 5 rivets for the panel and 7 for the lower aero skirt. Then remove the 5 screws along the wheel well skirt.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||09-28-2001||12:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by webbee:<BR><B>Wow those really are great looking! Is this a performance mod or for looks. Did you do both sides?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It is a performance and looks mod. It helps keep positive pressure in the air intake at driving speeds and allows cool air to pass into the engine compartment. Yes there is a panel on the passenger side too. Not sure if I'm going to use that as an oil cooler or a trans cooler. But right now it ducts cool air into the engine comartment.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroMaster88||09-28-2001||01:13 PM||||They look great!  Man do I want to do that to my car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||14
Z||000007||Rick 88||09-28-2001||01:23 PM||||Orief,<P>Do you think it would be possible to fab up a plastic panel for the inside of the drivers side scoop to seal it to the airbox?<BR>This would force all the air into the box itself. Has anyone done this with previous design side scoops? <P>I think Aus Fiero's planned side scoops show an internal duct that attaches directly to the airbox.<P>Rick 88||||reg||5
Z||000008||falconhulk||09-28-2001||02:09 PM||||Does 007DOUG doug make these?  Or did you just buy them from him?  I like these alot.  Any idea where to get them?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||09-28-2001||02:20 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by falconhulk:<BR><B>Does 007DOUG doug make these?  Or did you just buy them from him?  I like these alot.  Any idea where to get them?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sage is the person who actually makes them.<BR>007DOUG is the person who handles the purchase and shipping. See Dougs post in the "Mall" section. There is more pics of the panels, info, and prices.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/004338.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/004338.html</A> <P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rick88:<BR><B><BR>Do you think it would be possible to fab up a plastic panel for the inside of the drivers side scoop to seal it to the airbox?<BR>This would force all the air into the box itself. Has anyone done this with previous design side scoops?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes you can do that. You can go to a junkyard and get and intake from a car that fits the width. This is the piece that sits on the frame above the radiator. It is usually a wide scoop with a platic tube that went to the air cleaner box. Just mount it vertically behind the scoop and attach tube to the airbox. I had thought about doing this but I wanted some air to pass into the engine compartment for cooling.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||sqoach||09-28-2001||03:23 PM||||Wow! Those look great! I'll have to get me a pair when the time comes.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000011||Sage||09-28-2001||03:58 PM||||Oreif,<P>Those look great on there!  You did an excellent install.  The response you gave Rick88 is right on the money.  That is exactly what I told someone else when they asked about a direct hook up to the air box.  Haven't tried it myself yet, but believe it should work like a charm.<P>Thanks for keeping us up to date and posting your pics.  Oh by the way if anyone would like a low cost, highly effective interior mod, that adds a touch of "class" to their Fiero interior, I strongly recommend a set of Oreif's door emblems.  I have a set on both of my GT's, and they just look "right" in there!  Thanks Oreif!<P>Have a good one!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
